<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh taka ends weaker as importers chase dlr.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh taka ends weaker as importers chase dlr.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladesh's taka closed weaker at 42.2380/42.2480 to the dollar compared with the previous 42.2300/42.2400, dealers said.</p>
<p>Thjey said the taka eased on demand for dollars from importers of industrial raw materials after opening at 42.2350/42.2450.</p>
<p>Interbank call money rates closed at 3.75-4.25 percent against 4.0-4.25 percent previously.</p>
</text>
